    Suppose the input utility function is $\delta$-approximate to a monotone $\gamma$-submodular set function $f$, $c$ is a modular cost function, $\epsilon \in (0,1)$ is an error threshold. Let ${\rm OPT} =  arg\,max_{T \subseteq V}\{f(T)-c(T)\}$, after $\mathcal{O}(\frac{n}{\epsilon}\log \frac{n}{\gamma \epsilon})$ oracle calls to the $\delta$-approximate utility function,  Algorithm \ref{alg:up} outputs $\Tilde{S}$ such that
